// Title: PUA - WebBrowserPassView Execution
// Sigma ID: d0dae994-26c6-4d2d-83b5-b3c8b79ae513
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-08-20 | Modified: 2023-02-14
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1555.003
// Description: Detects the execution of WebBrowserPassView.exe. A password recovery tool that reveals the
//   passwords stored by the following Web browsers, Internet Explorer (Version 4.0 - 11.0), Mozilla
//   Firefox (All Versions), Google Chrome, Safari, and Opera
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/40b77d63808dd4f4eafb83949805636735a1fd15/atomics/T1555.003/T1555.003.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_webbrowserpassview.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "Web Browser Password Viewer" or FolderPath endswith "\\WebBrowserPassView.exe"
